{% comment %}
  Which set of drawings a menu group's names carry, named by the group rather than by the panel
  that draws it. 'menu-link-icon' takes the answer and draws one.

  The desktop panel names its sets by hand, per column, in `browse_columns`
  ('header-menu-drawer-links'): its columns are chosen one at a time and some of them deliberately
  carry no drawings - every Jewellery column, where 'icon-jewellery-type' draws the earrings and
  the necklaces but none of the rings, the men's pieces or the metal filters, so a set there would
  leave half the names with an empty box beside them. The mobile drawer has no such list: it walks
  the navigation itself, so it asks here instead. The rules below are the desktop panel's, which is
  what keeps the two menus drawing the same name the same way.

  Accepts:
  - group: {String} the group's title, e.g. "Shop by Style"
  - parent: {String} the top-level item's title, e.g. "Engagement"

  Outputs one of "ring-styles", "band-styles", "shapes", "stones", or nothing.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign icon_group = group | handle
  assign icon_parent = parent | handle

  comment
    A cut is a cut under any menu, and so is a stone, so those two are answered on the group alone.
    Style is not: Engagement's styles are settings and Wedding's are bands, and the two sets draw
    different things. "Women's" is the form Wedding's group takes in the navigation.
  endcomment
  comment
    Liquid reads `and` and `or` right to left and has no brackets to say otherwise, so the two
    tests that need both a parent and a group are nested rather than joined with `and`.
  endcomment
  assign icon_set = ''

  if icon_group == 'by-shape' or icon_group == 'shop-by-shape'
    assign icon_set = 'shapes'
  elsif icon_group == 'by-stone' or icon_group == 'shop-by-stone'
    assign icon_set = 'stones'
  elsif icon_parent == 'diamonds'
    if icon_group == 'lab-grown-diamonds'
      assign icon_set = 'shapes'
    endif
  elsif icon_parent == 'engagement'
    if icon_group == 'by-style' or icon_group == 'shop-by-style'
      assign icon_set = 'ring-styles'
    endif
  elsif icon_parent == 'wedding'
    if icon_group == 'by-style' or icon_group == 'womens'
      assign icon_set = 'band-styles'
    endif
  endif

  echo icon_set
-%}
